# ---- Claude Code: local tooling, not part of the thesis repo ----
# Project skills and settings stay on disk (they keep working for local sessions) but are
# not tracked -- they are AI-assistant tooling rather than thesis artifacts.
.claude/

# ---- Experiment artifacts (generated by training) ----
checkpoints/
runs/
runs_singletask/
results/
results_singletask/
abl_results/
abl_runs/
abl_logs/
sweeplogs/
# Ad-hoc driver/monitor scripts written on the compute box: hardcoded to /workspace, partly
# superseded, and duplicative of scripts/run_*.sh. The one thing that mattered in them (the
# OMP/MKL thread pinning) is documented in VASTAI_SETUP.md and set by the committed runners.
run_sweep*.sh
monitor_*.sh
*_driver.log
# NOTE: plots/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds source (plot_*.py) as well as the thesis
# figures, which are a deliverable and small (~2 MB). Ignoring the whole directory silently
# excluded newly added scripts/figures — git only applies ignore rules to UNtracked files, so
# already-tracked ones kept working and hid the problem.
# Superseded figure sets generated BEFORE the PPO/PT corrections (see FINDINGS.md §3): kept on
# disk for reference but not committed, so stale numbers can't be mistaken for results.
plots/figures_multitask_all5seeds/
plots/figures_singletask/
plots/vanilla_before_after.png
wandb/
videos/
*.pt
*.pkl
*.log

# ---- Derived data / exports ----
numeric_logs_csv/
numeric_logs_csv.zip

# ---- Knowledge-graph / tooling output ----
graphify-out/

# Keep source configs, README, requirements, scripts, and code tracked.
# To force-track a specific artifact (e.g. a paper figure): git add -f plots/final.png

# Local working docs: AI-assistant guide and rented-box setup notes. Kept on disk (CLAUDE.md
# is still loaded by local Claude Code sessions) but not part of the thesis repo.
CLAUDE.md
VASTAI_SETUP.md

# Thesis chapter drafts — kept local until reviewed by the supervisors.
THESIS_*.md

# --- Remote-run artifacts (regenerable; several hundred MB) ---
# Raw per-seed results pulled back from the vast.ai box. The figures in
# plots/figures_reinvestigation/ are committed; the inputs that produce them are not.
workspace/
gate_results/
gate_runs/
gate_logs/
rerun_results/
rerun_runs/
rerun_logs/

# Box-specific run playbook — machine/session specific, not part of the method.
VASTAI_RERUN.md

# Working session log — a debugging record, not a thesis document.
SESSION_LOG.md

# Figures from the superseded "rerun" sweep. That sweep ran with the joint-grad-clip and
# offline-eval-RNG defects present (REINVESTIGATION.md defects #12, #14), so the curves depict a
# protocol we retracted. Kept on disk, out of the repo. plots/figures_reinvestigation/ supersedes it.
plots/figures_rerun/

# Meeting prep -- a plain-language summary of FULL_PT.md for the supervisor meeting.
# Working note, not a thesis document; the citable record is FULL_PT.md.
MEETING_BRIEF.md

# Plain-language walkthrough of plots/figures_pt_full/ -- a reading aid for review meetings.
# Working note, not a thesis document; the citable record is FULL_PT.md.
FIGURES_GUIDE.md
